.TH tapectl-drive-cleaning-cartridge-add 1  "tapectl-drive-cleaning-cartridge-add " 
.SH NAME
tapectl\-drive\-cleaning\-cartridge\-add \- Register a cleaning cartridge
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtapectl drive cleaning\-cartridge add\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-rated\-uses\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISERIAL\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Register a cleaning cartridge
.PP
SERIAL is the serial the cartridge\*(Aqs chip reports (`drive status` shows it while the cartridge is loaded) or, when its chip cannot be read, any label that tells it apart; `drive cleaned \-\-cartridge` names it the same way. LTO Ultrium universal cleaning cartridges are rated for 50 cleanings, which is the default; `\-\-rated\-uses` says otherwise for a cartridge that carries another rating. A serial can be registered once.
.PP
`\-\-dry\-run` reports what would be registered and registers nothing.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output in JSON format
.TP
\fB\-\-rated\-uses\fR \fI<RATED_USES>\fR [default: 50]
How many cleanings the cartridge is rated for
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be done without making changes. Commands that cannot preview refuse the flag rather than ignore it
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose output
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
No live progress on stderr. Long operations (stage create, volume write/resume/verify/read\-slices, restore) still write their session log under <home>/logs/
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip ADR\-0008 Tier\-2 confirmation prompts. It never reaches a Tier\-3 refusal — those are facts, not risks to accept
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to config file.

NOTE: on its own this ALSO relocates the whole tapectl home to the config file\*(Aqs parent directory — database, keys, staging, stage reports. That is how every test harness gets an isolated home, so it still works, but it is surprising enough that it now warns. Use \-\-home when you mean "operate on a different archive", and \-\-config only to point at a config file inside that home.
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<HOME>\fR
tapectl home directory: database, keys, catalogs, stage\-reports, logs.

Defaults to ~/.tapectl. The config file is taken from <home>/config.toml unless \-\-config overrides it. Also settable as TAPECTL_HOME.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fISERIAL\fR>
The cleaning cartridge\*(Aqs serial
